# Observability

- Logging defaults (example env): `LOG_CHANNEL=stack`, `LOG_STACK=single`, `LOG_LEVEL=debug`.
- Structured Sentry logs use the `sentry_logs` channel (`driver` `sentry_logs`). The `sentry` channel reports Issues and spends the error quota.
- `App\Enums\LogCategory` registers Sentry channels (`jobs`, `feeds`, `debug`, `update_availability`) and sets `log_category`. Filter in Explore with `log_category:jobs` (or `feeds`, `debug`, `update_availability`).
- Turn logs on with `SENTRY_ENABLE_LOGS=true`, `SENTRY_LOG_LEVEL=warning`, and `LOG_STACK=single,sentry_logs`. DSN stays optional (`SENTRY_LARAVEL_DSN`).

## Log payload in category channels

- Keep the message constant; put changing values into context with `snake_case` keys and scalar values (`['count' => $count]`, not `"Удалено $count записей"`). Explore groups and charts by message.
- Context is the whole payload: `null` values are dropped and Laravel `Context` is not sent (it can hold customer data).
- Jobs log through `AbstractJob::log($message, $context)`. `job` and `memory_mb` are added automatically; job-wide attributes go in `logContext()`, the channel in `logCategory()`.
- Job lifecycle messages: `Старт`, `Успешно выполнено` (with `count` when there is one), `Ошибка выполнения` (level `error`, with `error`).
- Feeds log one `Фид сгенерирован` event: `feed`, `format`, `currency`, `size_bytes`, `duration_ms`, `memory_peak_mb`.

## Application metrics

Emit through `App\Metrics\ApplicationMetrics` (`\Sentry\traceMetrics()`). The SDK flushes metrics at the end of the request, command, or queue job. `enable_metrics` in `config/sentry.php` has no effect.

- `job.duration` — distribution, milliseconds, attribute `job`. Recorded by `MeasureJobDuration` for every `AbstractJob`, including failed runs.
- `availability.onec_rows` — gauge of rows received from 1C. The full-table sync does not emit it.
- `availability.products_unpublished`, `availability.products_published`, `availability.sizes_added`, `availability.sizes_removed` — counters for one availability run.
- `feed.duration` (distribution, ms), `feed.size_bytes` (gauge, bytes), `feed.memory_peak` (gauge, MB). Attributes: `feed`, `format`, `currency`.
- `payment.status` — counter on a status change to `SUCCEEDED`, `CANCELED`, or `WAITING_FOR_CAPTURE`, including COD created already succeeded. Attributes: `status`, `method`. `PENDING` is not sent.

## When adding error handling

- Prefer actionable logs with context (ids, order numbers, user id) over silent catches.
- If you introduce a new critical failure mode, consider whether it should be reported to Sentry.
